Task: engine/census.toml and the six classes
Class every function of the original in engine/census/census.toml, and check each class's evidence

The census now gives each of source/'s functions a class (Ported, Matched,
Native, Partial, Replaced or Missing) from rules by directory, file and
prefix, entries for single functions and the reference traces, and its
check fails when a class lacks its evidence: a trace or a traced caller,
a check against the original, a primitive the engine uses, what a
Partial leaves out, or a listed reason and stand-in for Replaced. An
owed reason excuses what is still lacking and is reported for the
completion track.

traced.tsv lists the 86 functions the reference scripts copy from
source/ (a body with the same names in the same order, so the fake
worlds' stand-ins are not counted). opence census --write generates it,
and --check also compares it and runs each script's own --check. The
census crate no longer counts its own doc comments as citations, and
the manifest reaches only the tests' source in the flake.

Checked: 17 class tests, the citation and real-tree tests, clippy -D
warnings on the census and cli crates, opence census --check on the
tree (81 Ported, 171 Matched owing evidence, 8249 Missing).
